     "body": "The A face carries the ethic that every conjugate operation answers to: Respect for Experience — right form and clear intention. Its body stays frozen and is linked, not rewritten: six movements — Life is awareness, experience; Form gives experience a world; Intention takes effect; Law carries entrusted power; The common world is apportioned; Experience renews the form. Its ground is the essay’s own: the fact of internality, disclosed in first-person immediacy — “I am undeniable, though nowhere to be seen.”",
